const faq = [
  ['What is the Biodance Bio-Collagen Real Deep Mask?', 'It is a two-piece hydrogel face mask that starts opaque and turns transparent as it sits on the skin. The brand lists low-molecular-weight collagen peptide, galactomyces, oligo hyaluronic acid and niacinamide as the key ingredients. It costs from $19.00 for a pack on the brand’s US store.'],
  ['How long should I leave a Biodance mask on?', 'The brand says to leave it on for 3 to 4 hours, or until it turns transparent, after toner or serum. You can also wear it overnight and remove it in the morning.'],
  ['Can I sleep in a Biodance mask?', 'The brand lists overnight use as a main way to wear it, and some reviewers sleep in it. I do not: my face gets cold and the mask disturbs my sleep, so I wear mine for 2 to 4 hours in the evening instead.'],
  ['What are the ingredients in the Biodance Bio-Collagen mask?', 'According to the brand’s page, the list starts with water, glycerin, acrylates copolymer and niacinamide, followed by carob gum and red algae extract. Later come galactomyces ferment filtrate, collagen extract, hydrolyzed hyaluronic acid and three probiotic ferments. The full list is in the article.'],
  ['Do Biodance collagen masks really work, and how long do results last?', 'Reviewers describe an immediate plump, dewy look, and a dermatologist quoted by BuzzFeed expects it to soften and hydrate and temporarily make skin look smoother. Most independent reviews I found say the effect lasts a day or two, not cumulatively. I treat it as a hydration treat, not an anti-aging treatment.'],
  ['Does the collagen in a face mask actually absorb?', 'The brand says its collagen has a molecular weight of 243 daltons, below the 500-dalton figure it cites for skin absorption, and calls its moisturizing result of +166% clinically proven. The page does not share how many people were tested or how, so I read those as brand claims. The hydration comes mainly from the humectants and the occlusive film.'],
  ['What is the difference between the pink, blue and purple Biodance masks?', 'The pink one is the Bio-Collagen Real Deep Mask, the blue one is the Hydro Cera-nol mask with ceramides and 50,000 ppm glacial water, and the purple one is the Rejuvenating Caviar PDRN mask with a 600,000 ppm caviar complex. The brand’s pages do not name the mask colors, so the colors come from retailer listings.'],
  ['Is the Biodance mask good for oily or acne-prone skin?', 'Some reviewers find the film-forming formula heavy for oily skin, and the collagen mask contains no acids or strong actives. If you break out easily, start with 3 to 4 hours instead of overnight and patch-test first.'],
  ['Is the Biodance mask safe during pregnancy?', 'The brand describes the formula as non-toxic and safe, including during pregnancy and breastfeeding, but advises consulting a doctor if you are concerned. This is not medical advice, so ask your doctor or dermatologist.'],
  ['How often can I use a Biodance mask, and how much do they cost?', 'The brand does not give a strict limit. I would use it once or twice a week as a treat, which also helps the budget: the brand lists packs from $19.00 for 4 masks, or about $4.75 per mask, and all sizes showed as sold out on the brand page when I checked in October 2026.']
];
