<article class="art">
<section class="p art-top"><a class="up arrow" href="/beauty/" style="color:#8A8A8A">Back to beauty</a>
<div class="art-head"><div><div class="up" style="color:#8A8A8A">Beauty · Masks · K-beauty · Updated October 2026</div><h1 class="hd">Biodance Bio-Collagen Real Deep Mask Review: Ingredients, How to Use, and the Blue and Purple Versions</h1><p class="serif stand">I adore these hydrogel masks, the pink collagen one, the blue one and the purple caviar one. Here is what is in each, how to wear them, what to realistically expect, and how the three differ.</p><div class="hand" style="transform:rotate(-2deg);font-size:34px;margin-top:10px">plump, dewy, a little ritual</div></div>
<div class="ph art-hero"><span>Image 1 · Hero<br><em>The pink Biodance collagen mask on my face, still opaque</em></span></div></div></section>
<section class="p art-grid"><div class="art-body">

<p>I love Biodance masks. They are the little ritual I look forward to: a jelly-like mask that starts opaque and slowly turns transparent on the skin. The pink Bio-Collagen is the famous one, and I am just as fond of the <strong>blue Hydro Cera-nol</strong> and the <strong>purple Caviar PDRN</strong>, so I cover all three here.</p>
<p>Because the hype is huge, I wanted the facts straight: Biodance’s official pages for the ingredients and claims, and public reviews for what other people say. I’m not a dermatologist, and this is not medical advice.</p>

<h2>How I use my Biodance masks: two years of little rituals</h2>
<p>I have normal skin, and I have been using Biodance masks since October 2024. The mask sits perfectly on my face and does not slide off. What I love most is my skin afterwards: luminous and soft, without any greasy residue.</p>
<p>I use all three versions, pink, blue and purple, depending on my mood. They all nourish really well and all aim at super hydration, so I cannot say one is clearly better than another. The list below shows when I reach for them.</p>
<p>One thing I do differently from the brand: I do not wear them overnight. My face gets cold and the mask disturbs my sleep. I wear mine for at least 2 hours, and ideally about 4. I would recommend them to anyone who loves treating themselves with little rituals, for a skincare night routine or just to feel more special, and I would buy them again.</p>
<div class="hand" style="transform:rotate(-2deg);font-size:34px;margin:6px 0 20px;color:#C2517A">a little ritual, to feel more special</div>
<h3>When I reach for them</h3>
<ul class="chk">
<li><strong>In winter,</strong> when I want extra hydration.</li>
<li><strong>During and after flights.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Before important events.</strong></li>
<li><strong>After a beach day.</strong></li>
<li><strong>As an evening self-care treat,</strong> for a skincare night routine.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Key takeaways</h2>
<ul class="chk">
<li><strong>My take after using them since October 2024:</strong> all three hydrate and leave skin luminous and soft with no greasy feel. I wear mine 2 to 4 hours, not overnight.</li>
<li>It is a <strong>two-piece hydrogel mask</strong> you wear for 3 to 4 hours, until it turns transparent, or overnight.</li>
<li>The pink collagen mask is built on <strong>collagen extract, galactomyces, hyaluronic acid and niacinamide</strong>, plus three probiotic ferments.</li>
<li>The brand claims <strong>+166% moisturization</strong> in a clinical test, but does not share the test details.</li>
<li>Independent reviews agree on an <strong>instant plump, dewy look</strong> and disagree on how long it lasts. Most say a day or two.</li>
<li>Pink = hydration and firmness, blue = ceramides and barrier comfort, purple = caviar and PDRN for glow.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Biodance Bio-Collagen Real Deep Mask at a glance</h2>
<ProductFacts title="Bio-Collagen Real Deep Mask, at a glance" rows={[['Good for','Dry, dull or tired-looking skin that wants a plump, dewy boost'],['Hero ingredients','Collagen extract, galactomyces ferment, oligo hyaluronic acid and niacinamide'],['Format','Two-piece hydrogel mask that turns transparent as it works'],['Size and price','From $19.00 on the brand’s US store (packs of 4, 8 and 16; all showed as sold out when I checked in October 2026)'],['How to use','After toner or serum, 3 to 4 hours or overnight; use the pieces on the neck too'],['FYI','Brand says hypoallergenic; the film can feel heavy on oily skin']]}/>
<p style="color:#8A8A8A;font-size:14px">Source: <a href="https://biodance.com/products/biodance-bio-collagen-real-deep-mask" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Biodance official product page</a>. Prices and stock change, so check the page before you buy.</p>
<div class="ph fig3"><span>Image 2<br><em>The pink, blue and purple Biodance masks side by side</em></span></div>

<h2>What’s inside: the full ingredient list</h2>
<p>I took the list from the brand’s official page and not from a retailer. In order, the pink Bio-Collagen mask reads:</p>
<details class="inci" style="margin:0 0 22px"><summary class="up" style="cursor:pointer;color:#8A8A8A;padding:10px 0">Show the full ingredient list</summary><p><em>Water, Glycerin, Acrylates Copolymer, Niacinamide, Ceratonia Siliqua (Carob) Gum, Chondrus Crispus Extract, Dipropylene Glycol, Betaine, Algin, Agar, Hydroxyacetophenone, 1,2-Hexanediol, Potassium Chloride, Caprylyl Glycol, Sucrose, Allantoin, Polyglyceryl-10 Laurate, Ethylhexylglycerin, Galactomyces Ferment Filtrate, Adenosine, Disodium EDTA, Pyrus Communis (Pear) Fruit Extract, Rosa Damascena Flower Water, Collagen Extract, Iris Florentina Root Extract, Cucumis Melo (Melon) Fruit Extract, Hedera Helix (Ivy) Leaf/Stem Extract, Butylene Glycol, Dipotassium Glycyrrhizate, Hydrolyzed Hyaluronic Acid, Lactobacillus Ferment, Bifida Ferment Filtrate, Lactobacillus Ferment Lysate, Tocopherol.</em></p></details>
<ProductInside intro="The brand builds the mask around hydration and a calming, barrier-friendly formula, held in a hydrogel film." items={[['Collagen extract','The brand’s headline ingredient, which it says is a very small collagen peptide. It appears in the second half of the list, so I treat it as a supporting player.'],['Galactomyces ferment filtrate','A ferment used for softness and a smoother, brighter look. It is one of the brand’s four key ingredients.'],['Hydrolyzed hyaluronic acid','A small hyaluronic acid that gives the brand’s “deep” hydration story, alongside glycerin and betaine.'],['Niacinamide','The fourth ingredient overall, used for tone and comfort.']]} also="adenosine, allantoin, pear, rose water, melon and ivy extracts, and three probiotic ferments"/>
<h3>Worth checking</h3>
<p>The mask has no strong acids or retinoids, which is why it is gentle, but it contains plant extracts and rose water, so patch-test if your skin is reactive. The film-forming base can feel heavy on oily or breakout-prone skin.</p>

<h2>Which skin concerns it suits</h2>
<table class="tbl"><tr><th>Concern</th><th>What to expect</th></tr>
<tr><td>Dryness and dehydration</td><td>The strongest point. Humectants and the film leave skin soft and dewy.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Dullness</td><td>A glow right after use. The brand says 90% of surveyed customers found skin brighter, without sharing the sample size.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fine lines</td><td>Plumping can soften the look of lines for a day or two, not permanently.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Visible pores</td><td>The brand says 100% of surveyed customers saw improved pores. Independent reviews call the effect temporary.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Redness and sensitivity</td><td>The brand says it is hypoallergenic and reduces redness. Patch-test anyway.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Oily or acne-prone skin</td><td>Some find it heavy. Try 3 to 4 hours before wearing it overnight.</td></tr></table>
<p style="color:#8A8A8A;font-size:14px">This table summarizes the brand’s claims and public reviews, not a clinical test.</p>

<h2>Does it work? What the brand and reviewers say</h2>
<p><strong>The brand’s numbers.</strong> Biodance says a clinical test showed a 166% increase in skin moisturization that continued after 150 hours. It also reports customer survey results: 100% said pore condition improved, 95% said skin felt moisturized, 90% said skin was brighter and 100% said redness improved. The page gives no number of participants or test design, so I treat these as encouraging marketing, not proof.</p>
<p><strong>The collagen question.</strong> The brand says its collagen has a molecular weight of 243 daltons, small enough to absorb. That is its own claim. What I see on my skin is hydration and a plump finish, which are real but temporary.</p>
<p><strong>Independent opinions.</strong> In Google’s results, reviewers describe an immediate dewy, bouncy “glass skin” look and a cooling, comfortable feel, with effects that usually fade after a day or two. Complaints include the long wear time, a fiddly two-piece shape and the cost of roughly $5 per mask. A dermatologist quoted by BuzzFeed expects it to soften and hydrate and temporarily make skin look smoother, but not to be a long-term anti-aging fix. Reddit threads are mixed, and some people are disappointed. I read these as honest expectations: it is a lovely hydration ritual, not a replacement for sunscreen, retinoids or other proven actives.</p>
<div class="ph fig3"><span>Image 3<br><em>The mask turning transparent after a few hours</em></span></div>

<h2>How to use it</h2>
<ul class="chk">
<li><strong>Cleanse, then apply toner or serum,</strong> so the mask can hold the moisture in.</li>
<li><strong>Place the bottom piece over the mouth,</strong> then the top piece over the eyes, and peel off the films.</li>
<li><strong>Leave it on for 3 to 4 hours</strong> until it turns transparent, as the brand says. I wear mine for at least 2 hours, ideally about 4, and not overnight.</li>
<li><strong>Remove gently</strong> and pat in what is left on the skin.</li>
<li><strong>Use the cut-outs on the neck</strong> or under the eyes, as the brand suggests, for extra hydration.</li>
<li><strong>In the morning, finish with sunscreen,</strong> like the <a href="/beauty/beauty-of-joseon-relief-sun-review/">Beauty of Joseon Relief Sun</a> or my <a href="/beauty/round-lab-birch-juice-sunscreen-review/">Round Lab Birch Juice</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Pink vs blue vs purple: which Biodance mask is for you?</h2>
<p>On my skin all three hydrate really well, so I choose by mood. The brand’s pages do not name the colors, so I matched the colors to the names from retailer listings. Always check the product name on the pack.</p>
<table class="tbl"><tr><th></th><th>Pink: Bio-Collagen</th><th>Blue: Hydro Cera-nol</th><th>Purple: Caviar PDRN</th></tr>
<tr><td>Key ingredients</td><td>Collagen extract, galactomyces, hyaluronic acid, niacinamide</td><td>Ceramides, glacial water (50,000 ppm), collagen, many hyaluronic acids</td><td>Caviar complex (600,000 ppm), PDRN and salmon egg extract, squalane</td></tr>
<tr><td>Brand focus</td><td>Hydration, firmness, pores</td><td>Soothing and barrier support</td><td>Glow and skin renewal</td></tr>
<tr><td>Brand test claim</td><td>+166% moisturization</td><td>+166% moisturization</td><td>+570% moisturization</td></tr>
<tr><td>Price</td><td>From $19.00</td><td>From $19.00</td><td>$19.00 (sold out when I checked)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Best for</td><td>Dry, dull skin; the classic</td><td>Dry, tight winter skin</td><td>Glow before an event</td></tr></table>
<h3>Blue: Hydro Cera-nol Real Deep Mask</h3>
<p>The brand calls Hydro Cera-nol its patented ingredient and pairs it with 50,000 ppm glacial water. Its list also includes five types of ceramides, cholesterol, phytosphingosine, shea butter and several hyaluronic acids. Full list from the brand’s page:</p>
<details class="inci" style="margin:0 0 22px"><summary class="up" style="cursor:pointer;color:#8A8A8A;padding:10px 0">Show the full ingredient list</summary><p><em>Water, Dipropylene Glycol, Glycerin, Cetyl Ethylhexanoate, Niacinamide, Xanthan Gum, Ceratonia Siliqua (Carob) Gum, Chondrus Crispus, Betaine, Panthenol, Hydroxyacetophenone, Ethylhexyl Olivate, Butyrospermum Parkii (Shea) Butter, Potassium Chloride, Caprylyl Glycol, Butylene Glycol, Cellulose Gum, 1,2-Hexanediol, Sucrose, Polyacrylate-13, Sodium Acrylates Copolymer, Glyceryl Stearate, Algin, Chondrus Crispus Extract, Glucomannan, Polyglyceryl-4 Oleate, Ethylhexylglycerin, Hydrolyzed Hyaluronic Acid, Hydrogenated Polyisobutene, Adenosine, Pyrus Communis (Pear) Fruit Extract, Disodium EDTA, Polyglyceryl-10 Laurate, Rosa Damascena Flower Water, Ethylhexyl Palmitate, Allantoin, Iris Florentina Root Extract, Sorbitan Isostearate, Cucumis Melo (Melon) Fruit Extract, Hydrogenated Lecithin, Hedera Helix (Ivy) Leaf/Stem Extract, Dextrin, Cetearyl Alcohol, Stearic Acid, Sodium Hyaluronate, Dipotassium Glycyrrhizate, Collagen Extract, Coriandrum Sativum (Coriander) Extract, Foeniculum Vulgare (Fennel) Seed Extract, Elettaria Cardamomum Seed Extract, Crocus Sativus Flower Extract, Hydroxypropyltrimonium Hyaluronate, Ceramide NP, Tocopherol, Ceramide NS, Cholesterol, Sodium Acetylated Hyaluronate, Phytosphingosine, Ceramide AP, Ceramide AS, Hyaluronic Acid, Hydrolyzed Sodium Hyaluronate, Sodium Hyaluronate Crosspolymer, Potassium Hyaluronate, Ceramide EOP.</em></p></details>
<h3>Purple: Rejuvenating Caviar PDRN Real Deep Mask</h3>
<p>The brand says this one has a 600,000 ppm caviar complex, PDRN and salmon egg extract, and reports a 570% moisturization increase and 100% of surveyed customers noticing a glow, again without the test details. Full list from the brand’s page:</p>
<details class="inci" style="margin:0 0 22px"><summary class="up" style="cursor:pointer;color:#8A8A8A;padding:10px 0">Show the full ingredient list</summary><p><em>Caviar Water, Water, Glycerin, Dipropylene Glycol, Cetyl Ethylhexanoate, 1,2-Hexanediol, Niacinamide, Propylene Glycol Dibenzoate, Chondrus Crispus Extract, Ceratonia Siliqua (Carob) Gum, Butyrospermum Parkii (Shea) Butter, Polyglyceryl-3 Methylglucose Distearate, Hydroxyacetophenone, Potassium Chloride, Algin, Chondrus Crispus Powder, Polyacrylate-13, Squalane, Glucomannan, Glyceryl Stearate, Cellulose Gum, Allantoin, Xanthan Gum, Sucrose, Ethylhexyl Olivate, Ethylhexylglycerin, Hydrogenated Polyisobutene, Sodium Acrylates Copolymer, Sodium Polyacryloyldimethyl Taurate, Adenosine, Lithospermum Erythrorhizon Root Extract, Sodium Phytate, Polyglyceryl-4 Oleate, Polyglyceryl-10 Laurate, Ethylhexyl Palmitate, Pyrus Communis (Pear) Fruit Extract, Sorbitan Isostearate, Rosa Damascena Flower Water, Sodium Polyacrylate, Salmon Egg Extract, Caviar Extract, Guaiazulene, Iris Florentina Root Extract, Cucumis Melo (Melon) Fruit Extract, Hedera Helix (Ivy) Leaf/Stem Extract, Tocopherol, Sodium DNA.</em></p></details>

<h2>My verdict</h2>
<p><strong>I reach for these</strong> in winter, during and after flights, before important events, after a beach day, or as an evening self-care treat. <strong>I’d look elsewhere</strong> if you want lasting wrinkle or pore changes: a sunscreen and proven actives do more, as in my <a href="/skin-guide/">skin guide</a>. And <strong>I’d be careful</strong> if you are acne-prone, avoid fish (the purple one contains caviar and salmon egg ingredients) or react to plant extracts: patch-test first.</p>
<p>For my full shelf, see the <a href="/beauty/morning-skincare-routine-dry-skin-winter/">morning routine</a> and the <a href="/beauty/axis-y-dark-spot-correcting-glow-serum-review/">Axis-Y glow serum review</a>.</p>

<blockquote class="quote">A mask will not change your skin forever, but it can change your evening.</blockquote>

<div class="callout"><div class="up">A note</div><p>I’m not a doctor. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, have a skin condition or take prescription skincare, ask your doctor or dermatologist before adding a new product.</p></div>

